Serialisation, Deserialisation, externalisation:

Externalisation internally extends the serialisable interface . This gives us the finer control over the serialisation process. 
Using serialisation, we dont have the control except using the transient keyword. But by making use of externalisable, we can have the complete control/

If we implement the externalisable interface, we should implement the methods writeExternal(ObjectOuput out) and readExternal(ObjectInput in).
-> If we want to serialise we should implement the writeExternal method and provide your custom implementation.
->If we want to deserialise we can make use of readExternal and provide the implementation.
-> These two methods may throw the i/0 Exception if there is any error in the write operation and may throw the classnotfound exception if the class is not defined.
